# DTF tier manifest: oci-manifests-reconcile-populated
#   artifact-keeper#1683 (1.12.0): the precondition for the oci_manifests
#   readers. On a populated repository the reconcile adds and removes exactly
#   the expected rows, and removes no row of a manifest a client can still
#   pull by digest.
#
# Profile-set: filesystem + gc.oci-manifests-reconcile-fast (the reconcile
# every 15 s). Everything is pushed over /v2 with curl; the shapes no client
# can produce today are made with SQL, each standing for a real history.
#
# THE POPULATION (OLP_GROUPS groups, default 30, about 19 manifests each,
# under image img-<g>; scr-<g> is a scratch image name)
#   A  image tagged                                              keep
#   B  image tagged, its only tag deleted                        absent
#   C  image tagged, the tag then moved to C2: C1 untagged with
#      its blob refs (a 1.11 reader serves it by digest)         keep (both)
#   D  index tagged, two children pushed by digest               keep (all)
#   E  index tagged, two children pushed under their own tags
#      that are then deleted (untagged children)                 keep (all)
#   F  index of indexes: leaf scr:l, middle index scr:m, top
#      index img:f; scr:l then scr:m deleted                     keep (all)
#   G  migrated (pre-#2457) index: its artifacts row moved to a
#      generic CAS key with SQL and its tag removed, its child's
#      tag and artifacts rows removed (kept only by the edge)    keep (both)
#   H  signature of A pushed by digest                           keep
#   J  image pushed, deleted by digest                           absent
#   K  image whose last tag was deleted, its row put back with
#      SQL (what a 1.11.0 replica's delete left)                 remove
#   L  image tagged, its row deleted with SQL (a push served by
#      a pre-268 replica)                                        add
#
# THE PASS
#   Every digest is fetched by digest under img-<g> (status before), every
#   row is aged an hour back with SQL (the reconcile skips rows younger than
#   600 s), the reconcile runs until two consecutive 15 s windows change
#   nothing, then every digest is fetched again (status after).
#
# THE GATES
#   (1) rows removed are exactly the K rows; (2) rows added are exactly the
#   L rows; (3) no removed row's digest answered 200 by digest before the
#   pass; (4) no digest's GET status changed across the pass except the L
#   images', which serve throughout.
#   On ak-backend:1.12.0 main before the readers slice (#4954's predicate):
#   gates 1 and 3 fail on C1, the F leaf and the G child, which a 1.11
#   reader still serves by digest.
#
# Wall clock: about 3 min for 30 groups.
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: about 2,000 requests back to back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem gc.oci-manifests-reconcile-fast"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
